Electromagnetic Waves and Antennas — Sophocles J. Orfanidis (@em-orfanidis: 0, is #reference, #part-of @em-sources) { r_2E9PTW5TH97W2B200A5XKHHNTQ
Sophocles J. Orfanidis, Rutgers University. Electromagnetic Waves and Antennas, 2016. [Official author/department page](https://ece.rutgers.edu/orfanidis) · [Book link supplied by that page](https://rutgers.box.com/s/rwzifofsu9slf8xy38f6uwhjd5gmn2q7).

Use this full advanced engineering companion for layered waves, transmission systems, waveguides, radiation and antennas, with substantial derivations and exercises. Compare reference planes, normalization and phasor signs before comparing numerical results.

On 29 October 2026 the official page linked the free book, errata and MATLAB toolbox and explained reclaimed author rights. The older Rutgers book URL returned 404 and automated Box retrieval was blocked; the complete current file and its detailed notice were not inspected. Free availability is not asserted to be a CC licence. Obtain the work through the official page and check its version; no toolbox or file is bundled.

